WEBVTT

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:36.110
This is Quetzalcoatl Sassassul-san,
from Antarctica.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:49.000
You'll sit next to Kimihara-san.

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:55.280
Kimihara-san, as her neighbor,
show her the ropes, okay?

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:02.840
Nice to meet you.

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:05.620
Y-Yeah... You, too.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:07.520
Now, let's start class.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:08.460
Stand.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:10.060
Bow.

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:13.260
I'm sorry!

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:14.860
No problem.

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:16.110
Take your seats.

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:29.120
Focus on the lesson, everyone.

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:40.090
<i>"I wish to drink it, but a mounted 
pipa player urges me on."</i>

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.000
<i>A classic poem...</i>

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:42.850
<i>Chinese, at that.</i>

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:44.430
<i>Would she know that?</i>

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:03.560
Kimihara-san!

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:07.230
What happened?!

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:09.950
Hime was startled.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:14.760
Hey, you're awake?

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:16.400
Are you okay?

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:23.830
She's not in here.

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:25.550
Whew...

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:27.520
Don't "whew" us.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.840
I mean, sure, she's scary, but...

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:33.180
If you faint at every little thing, 
you won't be able to come to school.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:39.480
That, too, but it could also be 
interpreted as discrimination.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:43.960
Oh, no! Discrimination has 
nothing to do with it!

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:47.110
It's just... snake people...

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:49.120
They bother you?

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.540
Better not let anyone 
else hear you say that.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.000
You're asking for trouble.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.060
Yeah...

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:57.050
Why do they bother you, anyway?

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:02.170
Remember that movie, 
<i>The Fear of Antarctica</i>?

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:05.090
Which one? The old one or the remake?

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:06.550
The one that's in color.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:10.850
We watched it at home 
when I was little, and...

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:33.370
<i>Who's there?!</i>

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:04.060
I get it.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:07.120
The one where the centaur heroine 
gets swallowed, huh?

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.890
Then it spits up her skin and
 disguises itself as her.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.370
They show that on TV sometimes.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:14.070
I kinda like it.

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:16.700
It's a movie that gets 
referenced a lot these days.

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:19.350
That whole thing is so far-fetched, though.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:22.420
It worked fine in the 
novel it was based on,

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:24.870
but the rough edges stand out 
a lot in the film version.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:28.030
The part where it spit up her 
skeleton was realistic, though.

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:31.050
Realistic in a sort of fake way.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:33.850
The production quality doesn't matter!

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:37.580
The point is, they've scared me 
ever since I saw that as a kid.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:38.850
What should I do?

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:41.320
You're asking us?

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:45.120
You have a problem with snake people 
because of a movie, right?

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:48.950
Then maybe you should watch it 
again and overcome your trauma?

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:51.520
Huh? I couldn't...

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:53.530
That'll just make her even more scared.

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:58.380
No, no. I get that it might've 
been scary to the baby princess,

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.740
but the film itself just an old B movie.

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:03.380
One that's a little... you know.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:07.490
If you watch it now, you'll think, 
"Wow, that's all it is?"

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:09.960
And your trauma will be gone!

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:12.180
You really think so?

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:14.810
You have nothing to lose, right?

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:23.310
By the way, did you guys carry me in here?

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:27.490
Do I look like a professional 
wrestler or weightlifter to you?

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:31.270
Jeez...

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:32.990
May I come in?

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:35.040
Yes.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.960
How are you feeling?

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:41.310
I'm all right now, thank you.

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:43.460
Shigetoki-san carried you here.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.560
Komori and Nekomi helped, too.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:50.090
Thank you very much.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:51.840
No trouble at all.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:06.600
Um... It seems I scared you.

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:08.860
Oh, no, not at all...

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:13.740
I was trying to smile, 
but I didn't do a very good job.

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:17.330
Really? What'd it look like? Let's see.

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:25.110
Yeah, that definitely packs a punch...

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:30.270
Maybe I can never fit in with 
all of you, after all...

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:34.880
H-Hey, come on... The thing with 
Hime is, there's this movie...

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:36.560
A movie?

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.890
Man, Kimihara sure is heavy.

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:44.890
But... she felt really soft.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:54.030
<b>Nurse's Office</b>

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:54.030
So, um... that's the story.

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:56.650
It's a terrible movie, really.

00:07:57.260 --> 00:08:00.600
I see. So a thing like that exists.

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:03.410
Now look!

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:05.290
Yeah, but...

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:08.270
It sounds highly interesting.

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:19.850
<b>Earth Sciences
 Prep Room</b>

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:15.690
I'm not allowed to enter the classroom,
 so I'll leave you here.

00:08:15.690 --> 00:08:17.700
Okay, got it.

00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:22.260
Yo!

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:28.140
It's unusual for you guys to 
come in here yourselves.

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:32.280
We cleaned the aquarium before, 
didn't we, Shrimp-senpai?

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:34.210
Who are you calling a shrimp?

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:38.140
Hello. I'll be joining you.

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:40.710
H-Hello...

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:45.200
Oh, wow! It's an Antarctican!

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:46.860
Pleased to meet you.

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:49.200
We can talk later.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:52.000
Vice Prez, you have a lot of 
videos stored here, right?

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:57.480
Found it!

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:00.680
Well, let's watch it!

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:01.660
Huh?!

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:03.130
What?

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:06.140
I'm not ready for this...

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:09.800
I'm putting it on.

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:16.300
No closing your eyes.

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:18.100
But...

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:20.920
Is this okay?

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:23.370
I just hope she doesn't get mad.

00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:34.900
<i>Alyssa, what's wrong?!</i>

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:39.710
Eyes on the screen.

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:41.970
<i>You aren't Alyssa!</i>

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.380
<i>Who have you turned into this time?!</i>

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:50.020
<i>Let's check your blood!</i>

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:57.020
S-Sorry!

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:05.410
<b>Play Movie | Audio & Subtitles | Chapter Select | Extras</b>

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:07.410
What did you think?

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:09.900
It was still scary!

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:11.520
It was scary.

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:13.790
Humans certainly are incredible.

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:16.810
To come up with a terrifying 
monster like that...

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:20.180
It ate people... Do you...

00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:24.850
No, no, don't be silly!

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.960
Please don't see me in the same 
light as a monster in a movie.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:30.180
We don't even have venomous fangs.

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:35.510
Unlike mammals that chew food,

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:37.920
our jaws aren't strong at all.

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:41.940
Even if one of us did bite you,
 it would feel like a kitten biting you.

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:45.360
Of course, we can't kill by
constricting like snakes do, either.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:50.550
And we don't have expanding rib cages,

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:52.280
so we can't swallow things whole.

00:10:54.840 --> 00:11:01.000
I can't even entertain the thought of eating 
someone I can speak with like this.

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:05.590
But if I'm seen as a 
monster like this one...

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:09.100
Well, there's nothing worse 
than that, for sure.

00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:11.840
Are you going to sue them or anything?

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:13.470
No.

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:18.190
I came here to put an end to
misunderstandings like this, after all.

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:23.520
I would be honored if you 
would be my friends.

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:25.500
Oh, it's nothing...

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:28.580
We'd be happy to be your friends.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:32.620
<b>Smile</b>

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:39.070
Hey, Hime!

00:11:39.070 --> 00:11:39.640
Hime!

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:40.710
Wha—

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:41.160
Princess!

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:46.930
<b>Antarcticans Are Like Walking Rumors.</b>

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:50.430
<b>But In the End, The Antarcticans' 
History and Roots Are a Mystery, Too.</b>

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:56.280
Quetzalcoatl-san.

00:11:57.450 --> 00:11:58.250
Yes?

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:00.810
I'd like to ask you a question. May I?

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:02.190
Sure.

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:03.320
I would, too!

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:04.060
Me, too!

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:07.580
Okay, okay. Everyone in order.

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:10.570
You're taking charge again?

00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:15.740
Well, can I go first, then?

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:18.670
Quetzalcoatl-san, you're a reptile...

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:21.260
or rather, not a warm-blooded 
creature, right?

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:24.900
How do you live in Antarctica, 
where it's so cold?

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:26.440
Good question.

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:30.000
There are two things you're mistaken about.

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:34.030
First, we are warm-blooded creatures.

00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:38.700
We're more like birds than primitive 
reptiles such as snakes.

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:42.920
Also, although we're commonly 
referred to as "snake people,"

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:45.770
that's only a vernacular term 
based on our appearance.

00:12:45.770 --> 00:12:49.080
Our actual link to snakes 
is believed to be quite tenuous.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:53.020
In the first place, if I didn't 
have the ability to maintain

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:56.460
a stable supply of energy to my brain, 
like other warm-blooded creatures,

00:12:57.090 --> 00:12:59.880
I wouldn't be able to talk 
to you all like this.

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:02.190
The brain consumes a lot 
of energy, after all.

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:09.220
Second, not all of Antarctica 
is buried under ice and snow.

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:13.500
Also, I grew up in an environment where 
it's expected that we'd have heating,

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:15.230
so I don't fare well in the cold.

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:17.590
My turn next.

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:22.100
Is it true that Antarcticans have controlled 
humanity from the shadows since ancient times?

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:23.770
Well...

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:28.300
Legends say that if you trace our 
civilization back several millennia,

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:30.640
our ancestors, 
who still crawled on the ground,

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:33.250
built underground cities 
all around the world.

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:35.290
It's unknown whether that's true, though.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:41.380
<b>*All of these books have been banned by the Department of 
the Interior's Bureau for the Conservation of Normal Society.</b>

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:41.380
<b>Plant Cultivators Have Decided That Our 
Next Rulers Will Be Snake People</b>

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:41.380
<b>Snake People Are Behind All 
the World's Conspiracies</b>

00:13:35.970 --> 00:13:39.350
But all the things written 
in so-called "occult books"

00:13:39.350 --> 00:13:41.020
are basically groundless.

00:13:41.580 --> 00:13:45.490
Our contact with humans 
began relatively recently,

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:47.010
and it has been very limited.

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:50.180
We differ on a spiritual level, 
for starters,

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:54.010
so it's difficult for us to comprehend humans,
much less control them.

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:57.010
We are not omnipotent.

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:59.850
Is it true that your kind ruled the Aztecs?

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:01.760
As it happened,

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:05.070
we did contribute some knowledge
and technology to their civilization,

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:08.500
but the rule was that we could not 
interfere in government affairs.

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:12.050
Humans and Antarcticans had minimal 
involvement with each other.

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:15.420
But humans are trying to get 
involved with you now?

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:16.740
Well, yes.

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:21.740
In the past, the very existence 
of Antarctica was unknown.

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:26.260
But now, it's easy to travel 
there in airplanes and boats.

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:28.640
But why'd you come to this school?

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:33.370
Because it's in a college town with an 
environment replicating the one I'm used to,

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:37.010
and I felt I could expect to 
find people of intelligence

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:40.890
and understanding who wouldn't 
greatly exceed a normal range.

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:45.150
<i>In other words, because we're 
slightly above average?</i>

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:49.160
Also, it's neither hot 
nor cold in extremes.

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:52.430
The wind gets pretty cold here in winter.

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:53.900
And it's hot in summer.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:57.440
So, pedantic questions aside...

00:14:57.440 --> 00:15:00.750
Quetzalcoatl-san, do you have a boyfriend?

00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:05.250
No.

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:08.500
I see! Just like me, then!

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:11.250
What type of guys do you like?

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:13.390
That's a difficult question.

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:16.810
Only our queen can lay eggs,

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:21.970
and most of our common citizens 
and warriors are female.

00:15:22.450 --> 00:15:24.780
Oh. I see.

00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:29.270
So I shouldn't really have 
romantic feelings...

00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:32.200
Shouldn't? Does that mean you do?

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:37.880
We do feel specialized emotions
 of favor toward certain individuals.

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:41.200
These things are hard to explain, though...

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:47.160
I'm not sure whether it's equivalent to 
friendship or romantic interest in humans.

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:53.810
I believe that, while we are fairly 
proficient in the natural sciences,

00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:57.840
our understanding of ourselves 
is less than that of humans.

00:15:58.460 --> 00:16:01.380
And our lack of knowledge about ourselves

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:03.470
is something we learned from humans.

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:06.480
This is starting to sound pedantic again...

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:07.860
Okay, next question...

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:09.480
I'm next!

00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:12.940
All right, time's up.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:16.310
Aw, I wanted to ask her what she eats.

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:18.600
You'll find that out at lunchtime.

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:21.690
But we still don't know 
anything about her at all!

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:24.140
You'll learn more in time.

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:27.090
All right, back to your seats!

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:36.250
<i>Now is the time to bring 
victory to our nation!</i>

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:39.010
<b>Human 
Evolutionary Theory</b>

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:45.650
<b>For Delicate Skin 
Seirei Cream</b>

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:45.640
<i>If you have pale skin, this is for you!</i>

00:16:46.430 --> 00:16:49.350
<i>Magical Girl Pretty Horn!</i>

00:16:49.970 --> 00:16:51.080
<i>Kazuko-san!</i>

00:16:51.470 --> 00:16:52.860
<i>No...</i>

00:16:53.150 --> 00:17:03.830
<b>Breaking</b>

00:16:53.150 --> 00:17:03.830
<b>Shocking! The Work of an Antarctican UFO?</b>

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:58.430
<i>In the case of an American research 
ship being sunk in Antarctic waters,</i>

00:16:58.430 --> 00:17:00.800
<i>the US government has evacuated Antarctica.</i>

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:03.820
<i>However, the government of 
Antarctica remains silent.</i>

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:09.800
<i>Other nations have expressed dismay 
in response to this incident,</i>

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:12.770
<i>but are resigned to watching and waiting 
to see what both nations do next.</i>

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:15.000
<i>Next in the news...</i>

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:23.390
What's that about?

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:26.350
Morning, Suu-chan!

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:28.680
Oh... Good morning.

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:31.200
So what's with that thing on your head?

00:17:31.560 --> 00:17:33.420
Is it Antarctican fashion?

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:36.690
Ah, no... It's, um...

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:38.360
The news...

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:40.070
Hm? What?

00:17:40.070 --> 00:17:43.430
Oh, the thing about the 
American ship that was sunk?

00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:44.540
And?

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:49.240
I felt it would be best to avoid drawing 
attention to myself, if at all possible.

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:51.450
<i>Avoid</i> drawing attention?!

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:54.540
Lower your head.

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:56.790
How are you avoiding attention?

00:17:56.790 --> 00:17:57.930
Idiot! Don't do that!

00:18:00.020 --> 00:18:03.520
It's all right. A little overreaction 
like this is no big deal.

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:05.930
It doesn't look that way to me...

00:18:06.430 --> 00:18:09.640
More importantly, 
was that what you call a "retort"?

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:12.320
Uh, that's not more important...

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:15.060
Look, you're not some 
burglar who needs a mask.

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.170
I felt I should at least try...

00:18:17.170 --> 00:18:20.450
Yeah, no. First of all, 
no one can hurt you right now.

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:24.780
Also, it was an American ship, 
so we should be fine here.

00:18:25.070 --> 00:18:28.860
Do you think that's true? 
They were still humans.

00:18:28.860 --> 00:18:30.830
Well, yeah...

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:34.340
Anyway, Suu-chan, you always 
wear clothes like that, huh?

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:37.560
I do wear a different one each day...

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:39.050
Does it smell?

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:41.680
That's not what I meant!

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:45.300
Come to think of it, you guys are 
always dressed that way on TV, too.

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:49.700
Apparently, its origins lie 
in human monk garments.

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:53.960
By the way, the hems are short in 
following with advice I received

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:57.630
from the lady ambassador,
 who is also my language teacher.

00:18:58.310 --> 00:19:00.470
It does look very girlish!

00:19:00.470 --> 00:19:04.610
Teacher? So you learn a 
language by studying it?

00:19:04.610 --> 00:19:06.490
Not through sleep-learning or something?

00:19:06.940 --> 00:19:10.670
Of course. Memory works 
in essentially the same way

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:12.870
for all animal species, including insects.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:16.560
My teacher taught me everything from 
mannerisms to general knowledge,

00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:19.060
all with great passion.

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:20.870
You've had it rough, huh?

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:25.890
Oh, no. I've had so much help, 
I couldn't feel more guilty.

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:28.510
Are you required to dress like that?

00:19:28.970 --> 00:19:30.320
No, not at all.

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:33.780
Then would you like to come 
look at clothes with us?

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:47.140
You look surprisingly 
good in girly clothes.

00:19:47.610 --> 00:19:49.650
Why don't you try some on, Nozomi-chan?

00:19:50.510 --> 00:19:51.700
Me?!

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:55.710
You look like a boy in drag!

00:19:56.650 --> 00:19:59.540
It's fine! If we just comb your hair out...

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:08.020
You both look so handsome!

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:11.760
I think it's a bit too open 
in the seat, though...

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:15.120
That one's meant for trying on, 
so the tail opening is one-size-fits-all.

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:18.400
If you buy it, we'll alter 
it to fit you perfectly.

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:20.010
Hang on!

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:22.840
I've never altered anything 
for a snake person before!

00:20:22.840 --> 00:20:24.900
If you refuse, you'll be sent 
to a correctional clinic.

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:27.430
If you can't do it, just get the owner.

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:33.410
What do you think?

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:35.900
It's cold and delicious.

00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:37.580
Still...

00:20:37.590 --> 00:20:41.590
<b>Furukanata VISION</b>

00:20:37.590 --> 00:20:41.590
<b><i>Strained relations between the US and Antarctica continue. 
US government considering recall of ambassador to Antarctica.</i></b>

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:41.400
Everyone is being so kind, 
even after that terrible incident.

00:20:45.710 --> 00:20:48.690
Well, it's not like that was your fault.

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:52.980
They don't even have proof 
Antarctica's government did it, right?

00:20:53.320 --> 00:20:54.580
That's true.

00:20:54.580 --> 00:20:58.850
We are capable of protecting ourselves 
from beasts and belligerent peoples—

00:21:00.140 --> 00:21:02.980
I'm sorry. I can't say any more than that.

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:05.610
Uh, I don't think you need to.

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:07.490
A-hup.

00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:10.370
Well, anyone up for a movie?

00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:12.710
One of your choosing?

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:16.790
What? It's a really popular one! 
I'm sure it'll be good!

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:20.290
I don't want to see anything violent...

00:21:20.290 --> 00:21:22.710
You're not supposed to think 
about that. Just enjoy it.

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:27.260
<b>Bonds on the Battlefield</b>

00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:28.960
See? That was pretty good, right?

00:21:30.980 --> 00:21:33.390
It certainly made me think.

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:37.410
Huh? It's just meant to entertain. 
There's nothing to think about.

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:41.660
I hope to deepen my understanding enough 
to think the same way someday.

00:21:42.240 --> 00:21:44.560
Why? For work?

00:21:44.910 --> 00:21:48.690
Normal Antarcticans would 
see it as their duty.

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:52.660
But I'm not normal, and I think...

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:54.720
that's why I'm here.

00:21:57.780 --> 00:22:00.600
Wow, nice line! Like something out of a movie!

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>Is Being Able to Retrace One's Past and 
Ancestors A Reason to Be Happy or Unhappy?</b>

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>Does Getting a Job Doing What 
You Love Really Bring Happiness?</b>
